<p class="copy">
	Making up the majority of the tonnage in most national navies, frigates are the fleet's workhorse warships. Heavily armored and well armed, they form the backbone of fleet formations and are often deployed in small tactical battlegroups. Unlike smaller <?php echo sf_lore_link('corvettes', 'corvettes'); ?>, which are typically built around a specific mission, frigates are generalized combat vessels designed to bring heavy firepower and thick armor to the decisive engagements of void warfare.
</p>
<p class="copy">
	As ships-of-the-line, frigates are built for function and endurance rather than comfort. They often lack the crew amenities, diplomatic facilities, and civilian luxuries found aboard larger vessels. Few are equipped with <?php echo sf_lore_link('lorentz-field-generator', 'LFGs'); ?>, leaving frigates dependent on <?php echo sf_lore_link('stellar-carriers', 'stellar carriers'); ?> for inter-system deployments.
</p>
